{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HjPfGHvAXSkQ67nHfi9VvA","type":"tool_result","content":"TALLY_BRIEF=/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/3c71c1e798dfa264ce35280543c9451ed1a64be0e32bed1d159e261360e0603f.json\n---\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task bench-harness: Measurement harness: honest client and counterbalanced matrix. Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"bench\\\",\\\"tests\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched by any task commit, including a path later deleted or renamed, must remain inside them. If completion requires an authority-surface path, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-authority\\\",\\\"paths\\\":[...]} as the final message; if the task is impossible, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"impossible\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"...\\\"} as a claim for the judge, never as a verdict. Before changing code, read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane. Definition of done, in this order: (1) run this task's acceptanceCriteria commands and see them pass; (2) `git add` every file you changed, within the write boundary stated above; (3) `git commit` on the branch already checked out in the assigned worktree; (4) run `git status --porcelain` and confirm it prints nothing before you exit. Ownership validation reads committed history only: an exit with uncommitted changes fails the attempt (\\\"agent left uncommitted changes; commit the task before ownership validation\\\") and the uncommitted work is discarded.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:3517aea133a5aad9239e2a450cfd7fcfac0af4eddf36bf6bcb389826e0947286\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"python3 -m py_compile bench/fn-stream-client.py && bash -n bench/run-matrix.sh && python3 -m unittest tests.test_bench_client -v\"],\"description\":\"Client compiles, separation test passes, matrix script is syntax-clean.\",\"id\":\"bench-honest-client\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"bench\",\"tests\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"A client whose prefill number is a measurement, not a proxy\",\"A matrix whose every number carries its protocol\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"Write bench/fn-stream-client.py and bench/run-matrix.sh per spec claims 6.2 and 6.3 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6). The client measures per-request time-to-first-token client-side AND scrapes the server metrics endpoint to separate scheduler queue wait from prompt processing — the reference harness's client published a prefill column that duplicated its first-token column (specs/flashnext/evidence/nix-strix-halo.md section 4.4); ours must not. Emit CSV with explicit column semantics in a header comment, plus a sha256 fingerprint of every completion's token ids. run-matrix.sh: arms interleaved A-B-B-A, three loads per arm, medians reported, depth series 0, 10240, 102400 tokens, speculative decoding on and off arms, results committed under results/ and a bench.json receipt {loads_per_arm, counterbalanced:true, arms, fingerprints}. Add tests/test_bench_client.py: feed the client parser a fixture with known queue and processing times and assert the two columns separate them. Boundaries: touch only bench/ and tests/.\",\"id\":\"bench-harness\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/nix-strix-halo.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/receipts-verify.py\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:3a8882e61c9b2ce9ef7a7904e06778f0284df952e4a68deb4f8e6e1caba1a225\",\"title\":\"Measurement harness: honest client and counterbalanced matrix\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"754e1118d0ce0414aa2f72fb2a7fdaa668e857cc\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-b3312d8e025f/bench-harness\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"bench\",\"tests\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/bench-harness-3a8882e61c9b2ce9\",\"taskId\":\"bench-harness\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/b3312d8e025f/bench-harness\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[],\"attemptReceipt\":{\"lateRecheckCommentIds\":[],\"preparedCommentIds\":[],\"recheckTruncated\":false,\"rechecked\":true,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"local-jsonl\",\"path\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering-v1.jsonl\",\"preparedCursor\":0,\"recheckedCursor\":0,\"registrationId\":\"01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff\"}},\"machineDiagnoses\":[],\"machineOutcomes\":[]}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bfb6510-93c6-4f5c-80df-1deb6ae6c180","uuid":"51d09525-8836-4bce-9294-12596e307558","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:24:50.276Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"TALLY_BRIEF=/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/3c71c1e798dfa264ce35280543c9451ed1a64be0e32bed1d159e261360e0603f.json\n---\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task bench-harness: Measurement harness: honest client and counterbalanced matrix. Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"bench\\\",\\\"tests\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched b