rst_token is None else first_token - start\n871:        decode = None if ttft is None else max(0.0, duration - ttft)\n875:i.e. when N concurrent workers are simultaneously unleashed. `first_token` is\n878:**vLLM scheduler queue wait**, prompt prefill, the first decode step, and SSE\n886:time-to-first-token and total request time. In the CSV, prefill time is the\n887:TTFT proxy: it includes queueing plus prompt prefill plus the first decode\n888:step. Decode time is total time after TTFT.\n893:column name**. `prefill_mean_s` appears in `FIELDS` at `:52`, adjacent to the\n894:three `ttft_*` columns at `:49–51`, so a CSV consumer reasonably reads it as an\n896:`prefill_mean_s` as prefill time is invalid at concurrency > 1.**\n898:**[S] Corroborating absence:** grepping the file for `prefill|ttft|queue`\n900:`vllm:time_to_first_token_seconds`, or any scheduler-queue histogram. The client\n901:never queries server-side telemetry. Separating prefill from queueing requires\n1272:   Line 297 is character-identical to line 294; both are `statistics.mean(ttfts)`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
