{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FfeU68ubJKJ2EVCEW4eVm3","type":"tool_result","content":"M  bench/fn-stream-client.py\nM  tests/test_bench_client.py\n--- staged ---\n bench/fn-stream-client.py  | 47 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------\n tests/test_bench_client.py | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 2 files changed, 66 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bfb6510-93c6-4f5c-80df-1deb6ae6c180","uuid":"018cb7cb-0371-407c-88a6-9ae465a35fa2","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:28:27.689Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"M  bench/fn-stream-client.py\nM  tests/test_bench_client.py\n--- staged ---\n bench/fn-stream-client.py  | 47 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------\n tests/test_bench_client.py | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 2 files changed, 66 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYDtqe3uxLqE5qjTRxDn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TLcn5c4uTsAjh1qcAgX6uB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nbench-harness: a failed scrape is an absence, not a lifetime mean\n\nThe harness and its matrix were already present and passing on this lane's\nbase (banked at 1436c83). Reconciling them against spec claims 6.2/6.3 turned\nup two places where the client published a number that was not a measurement\nof what its column name promised — the same class of defect as the reference\nharness's prefill_mean_s (evidence/nix-strix-halo.md §4.4), which is the whole\nreason this client exists.\n\n1. A failed bracketing /metrics scrape was passed to the split as {}, so the\n   histogram delta was taken against a zero baseline and returned the engine's\n   WHOLE-LIFETIME mean. main() printed \"queue/prefill will be empty\" while the\n   CSV carried that lifetime figure in queue_wait_s and prefill_s. Measured on\n   a synthetic 5000-request lifetime: 20.0 s queue / 0.8 s prefill, published\n   as if they were this batch's. A missing bracket now reaches the split as\n   None and both columns go empty, with prefill_source recording\n   scrape-unavailable — a scrape failure is a different fact from \"the engine\n   does not expose this histogram\", and both differ from a number.\n\n2. fingerprint_of([]) returned sha256 of the empty input, so every request that\n   produced no tokens shared one constant digest. The matrix's divergence\n   analysis (Phase B/D) would have read a set of silent requests as agreeing\n   witnesses. An empty sequence now fingerprints to the empty string; the\n   matrix's fingerprint reducers already filter empties.\n\nThe CSV header comment states both absences, so the protocol still travels with\nevery column. Regression tests added for each. Acceptance criteria pass; the\nother four test modules and scripts/receipts-verify.py stay green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit --no-pager log --oneline -1; echo \"--- porcelain ---\"; git status --porcelain; echo \"[clean]\"","description":"Commit on the assigned branch"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":283,"cache_read_input_tokens":92939,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":283},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bfb6510-93c6-4f5c-80df-1deb6ae6c180","uuid":"fa5d594a-aa5e-4ba7-8902-1aa870ad3e4b","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:28:39.313Z","request_id":"req_011CeYDtpvtApfxmKrhjEHrT"}
