{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYDupGyEjXc7UMNuVreA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Committed `09a976b` on `tally-work/flashnext-b3312d8e025f/bench-harness`; `git status --porcelain` is empty.\n\n## What I found\n\nThis was a reconcile attempt, and the deliverable was **already present and passing** on the lane's base — `bench/fn-stream-client.py`, `bench/run-matrix.sh`, and `tests/test_bench_client.py` were banked at `1436c83`, an ancestor of `HEAD`. I verified the existing work against every clause of the goal before touching anything: client-side per-request TTFT plus `/metrics` scraping for the queue/prefill split, CSV header comment with column semantics, sha256 token-id fingerprints, A-B-B-A interleave (with `LOADS_PER_ARM=3` the schedule is `A B B A A B`), three loads per arm, medians in Phase B, depth series `0 / 10240 / 102400`, spec-on/spec-off arms, and a `bench.json` receipt carrying `loads_per_arm`, `counterbalanced`, `arms`, `fingerprints`. All satisfied.\n\nRather than commit churn, I audited for real defects and found two — both cases where the client published a number that wasn't a measurement of what its column name promised, which is the exact §4.4 failure mode this task exists to prevent:\n\n1. **A failed pre-scrape became a zero baseline.** `main()` set `before = {}` on scrape failure, so `hist_delta_mean` differenced against zero and returned the engine's *whole-lifetime* mean. Meanwhile stderr printed \"queue/prefill will be empty\" — they weren't. I reproduced it: a synthetic 5000-request lifetime yielded `queue_wait_s = 20.0`, `prefill_s = 0.8`, published as that batch's figures. A missing bracket now arrives as `None`, both columns go empty, and `prefill_source` records `scrape-unavailable` (a distinct fact from \"the engine doesn't expose this histogram\").\n\n2. **`fingerprint_of([])` returned sha256-of-nothing.** Every token-less request shared one constant digest, which the matrix's divergence analysis in Phases B/D would have read as agreeing witnesses. Empty sequences now fingerprint to `\"\"`; the matrix's reducers already filter empties, so the consumers needed no change.\n\nAdded a regression test for each and documented both absences in the CSV header comment.\n\n## Verification\n\nAcceptance criteria pass (12 tests, up from 10). I also ran the four sibling test modules and `scripts/receipts-verify.py` — all green, so nothing regressed outside the client. Note that `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` fails on this tree for an unrelated pre-existing reason (no `tests/__init__.py`); I ran the modules by name instead.\n\nChanges stayed inside the `bench` / `tests` write boundary. I did not touch `results/` — the matrix writes there at runtime, and it's outside the boundary regardless."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":953,"cache_read_input_tokens":93222,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":953},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bfb6510-93c6-4f5c-80df-1deb6ae6c180","uuid":"06eb2515-d78b-416c-ae41-6c944b9aca4f","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:28:54.158Z","request_id":"req_011CeYDuo9zxpYYiCjpMRFnb"}
